  "title": "Circumcision",
  "description": "A circumcision removes the foreskin covering the tip of your penis. This brief outpatient procedure takes 20-30 minutes and can be performed at any age. You're given local anesthesia for comfort. Afterwards, you'll have swelling and soreness for 1-2 weeks. Activity restrictions vary by age, children usually resume normal play within days, while adults need 1-2 weeks before strenuous activity. Sexual activity should wait 4 weeks. Your doctor provides clear wound care instructions. Most people heal perfectly without complications. Circumcision may be performed for religious reasons, phimosis (tight foreskin), or personal preference.",
